// A live Strudel (TidalCycles-in-JS) pattern, linked by the "pad" and "kit" tracks.
// The engine plays it on them while the transport rolls, locked to the beat — edit +
// save to hear it change live.
//
// `.label(...)` names the lane a part plays on. A label matching a strudel track's
// name lands there — "Pad" on the "pad" track, so it plays through that track's chain
// and mixer strip. A label no track declares still plays, on the file's first track by
// name ("kit"); so does an unlabelled part.
//
// What `s(...)` means is the event's business: a name found as a sample — in your
// project's `samples/` folder, $DIRT_SAMPLES or $STRUDEL_SAMPLES — is a one-shot,
// anything else is a note for the lane's instrument ("sawtooth" on "pad").
stack(
  note("c e g c5").s("sawtooth").slow(2).label("Pad"),
  sound("bd hh sn hh").label("Kit"),
)
